+<!--
+  Copyright (c) 2026, Intel Corporation. All rights reserved.
+-->
+
+# ocs2_mobile_manipulator_nonros scripts
+
+Helper scripts for the non-ROS ALOHA dual-arm demo.
+
+## Overview
+Three helpers drive the dual-arm demo:
+- `run_aloha_dual_arm.sh` — launches the two MPC/MRT arm nodes together.
+- `mujoco_viewer.py` — one MuJoCo window showing both arms and the tabletop box.
+- `aloha_act_publisher` — test driver that streams a target trajectory to the nodes and viewer.
+
+Data flows over the ECI shared-memory transport: the nodes publish each arm's
+joint state, the publisher supplies gripper targets, and the viewer renders them.
+
+## Dependencies
+- MuJoCo and hardened XML parsing for Python (`pip install mujoco==3.10.0 defusedxml>=0.7.1`).
+- `libshmringbuf.so` on `LD_LIBRARY_PATH` (e.g. `/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu`)(`sudo apt install libshmringbuf-dev plcopen-databus-dev`).
+
+## Building
+This package uses CMake. To build:
+
+```bash
+cd [your path to ocs2 workspace]
+colcon build --packages-select ocs2_mobile_manipulator_nonros
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+### Launch both arms
+```bash
+cd [your path to ocs2]/ocs2_robotic_examples/ocs2_mobile_manipulator_nonros/scripts
+./run_aloha_dual_arm.sh
+```
+Resources are auto-discovered via `AMENT_PREFIX_PATH`; override with
+`NODE_BIN` / `TASK_FILE` / `URDF_FILE` / `LIB_FOLDER`.
+
+### MuJoCo simulation
+One viewer process loads a MuJoCo scene XML and displays both vx300s arms plus the
+box. It runs full physics, so the grippers make real contact and can grasp and lift
+the box. Each arm follows its own shared-memory joint block; each gripper follows a
+separate gripper block.
+
+```bash
+SCENE=[your path to ocs2]/ocs2_robotic_examples/ocs2_mobile_manipulator_nonros/aloha_dual_arm_viewer.xml
+cd [your path to ocs2]/ocs2_robotic_examples/ocs2_mobile_manipulator_nonros/scripts
+python3 mujoco_viewer.py "$SCENE"
+```
+Arm-joint prefixes default to `vx300s_left` / `vx300s_right` (override with
+`--left-prefix` / `--right-prefix`); refresh rate with `--rate`. Any equivalent
+scene XML works — its includes and meshes are resolved relative to it. Startup
+order does not matter: each block is opened lazily, so the viewer can run before
+the publishing nodes.
+
+### ACT target + gripper publisher
+Streams a 14-value ACT target (both arms + both grippers) to the nodes and viewer,
+and prints each arm's live end-effector pose.
+
+```bash
+TRAJ=[your path to ocs2]/ocs2_robotic_examples/ocs2_mobile_manipulator_nonros/test/target_trajectories_with_grippers.txt
+BIN=[your path to ocs2 workspace]/install/ocs2_mobile_manipulator_nonros/lib/ocs2_mobile_manipulator_nonros/aloha_act_publisher
+"$BIN" --traj "$TRAJ"          # play once
+"$BIN" --traj "$TRAJ" --loop   # loop forever
+```
+The trajectory file is a whitespace-separated text table with a column-name header
+row; the publisher looks up columns by name, so column order may change safely.
+With `--loop`, the publisher bumps a loop index on the `world_reset` shm block at the
+start of each pass; the viewer resets the tabletop box to its keyframe pose on every
+change, so each pass starts from a clean scene instead of accumulating the box's drift.
+The trajectory path must be absolute — otherwise the publisher falls back to a single
+static pose. Confirm loading with `[act_publisher] playing ... trajectory points`.
+Other options: `--seconds N` static run duration, `--left` / `--right` arm
+prefixes, positional numbers or `--qpos` to force a single static target.
+
+## Folder Structure
+- `run_aloha_dual_arm.sh` - dual-arm launcher
+- `mujoco_viewer.py` - MuJoCo simulation viewer
+- `aloha_act_publisher` - trajectory / gripper test driver (built to `lib/ocs2_mobile_manipulator_nonros/`)
diff --git a/ocs2_robotic_examples/ocs2_mobile_manipulator_nonros/aloha_dual_arm_viewer.xml b/ocs2_robotic_examples/ocs2_mobile_manipulator_nonros/aloha_dual_arm_viewer.xml
